And I (still) think it's a blessed +2 long sword named Frost Brand (not
Frost brand as the spoilers and some other posters say). Once a priest or
a wizard has a decent weapon, you can finish with them 3 out of 4 times.
The GDSM is nice, but in case of problems you can always engrave Elbereth,
and after some time you have collected enough AC anyways. The weapon is
needed for wimpy characters: it's very annoying to fight a monster that
regenerates faster than you can remove it's hit points with a simple athame
or mace or scalpel...
Once you have a good weapon, you should only die because of extreme bad luck
or gross stupidity. That is why my second wish is for a blessed amulet of life
saving. Once I had that, I never failed to finish the game.

Ps. In my last game I used the blessed bag of holding trick for the first time
(and yes, you can carry boulders if you do that). I found out that you can
repeatedly do this, but after the third time, the bag gets so light that the
calculations of hit chances go wrong: as long as I was holding the bag, I
always missed the monster. So I had to drop it in every fight. Up to the
point something swallowed me. I dropped my bag again, and killed the monster.
Whin I wanted to pick it up again, I couldn't. It seems like it recalculated
the weight from the contents. And I had things in there like 1000 rocks, that
were to heavy to take out, so I couldn't even empty the thing. Took me some
time to get that working again. So, note to the dev. team: when you fix the
bag of holding weight code, probably to a system where blessing allows you to
put in more, and keep the gain reasonable, don't forget to take out this
recalculation effect.



